WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.733
It shows you where the trouble most likely is.

3
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:11.801
You hold the grown-up page. Your child writes on the other page: their name, ten letters, and two words.

4
00:00:12.251 --> 00:00:15.856
Here is the one thing to know. Watch the pencil, not the paper.

5
00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:22.867
A letter can look fine on the paper and still be made from the bottom up. You only see that while it is being written.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.825
There are three things to mark.

7
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:30.796
Part A. While your child writes their name, look at the sitting, the pencil hold, and the helper hand.

8
00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:36.945
Part B. For each of the ten letters, mark it if the pencil starts at the green dot on your page.

9
00:00:37.395 --> 00:00:39.101
For this letter, that is the top.

10
00:00:40.466 --> 00:00:43.305
For this one, it is high on the right, curving back.

11
00:00:44.732 --> 00:00:50.208
Part C. When the row is finished, mark each letter that sits on the line and is the right height.

12
00:00:50.658 --> 00:00:54.406
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just watch and mark.

13
00:00:54.856 --> 00:01:00.573
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

14
00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:07.397
It points to the most likely sticking point: the pencil hold, the starting places, or size and the line.

15
00:01:07.847 --> 00:01:12.993
Write the three numbers on the page. Keep both pages. You will put them beside day ten.
